    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented both functions in `app/network.py`. A check script using stub transports confirmed each requirement, and `pytest -q` passes (3 tests).\n\n**`configure_hub_http(transport=None)`** uses huggingface_hub's `set_client_factory` to make every `HfApi` share one HTTP client. That client:\n- has a connect timeout of 5s and read, write and pool timeouts of 60s;\n- sends `X-Acme-Job: nightly-sync` on every request, alongside huggingface_hub's own headers (its user agent was still present in the check);\n- uses `transport` when one is given;\n- keeps huggingface_hub's own request hook, so offline mode, request IDs and debug logging still work.\n\n**Something to know about the timeouts:** in 2.0.0 the library passes `timeout=None` on each request, for example in `model_info`. In `httpx2`, that turns timeouts off completely and ignores the client's default. To stop that, a small request hook sets our timeouts on every outgoing request. This also overrides the few timeouts the library sets itself, which matches \"every request\" in your spec.\n\n**`current_revision(repo_id)`** returns `HfApi().model_info(repo_id, revision=\"main\").sha`. On a connection failure or timeout it logs a warning on `app.network` and returns `None`. Other errors still raise; a 404 raised `RepositoryNotFoundError`.\n\n**Cleanup:** my temporary check script `_check.py` is still in the project root because deleting it needed your approval. You can delete it, or tell me to.\n\nNo dependencies were added. `httpx2` is already installed as a dependency of huggingface-hub 2.0.0."
